    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01JDWZTJBSE3EBP3NW2CR9T6RT\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to add a tag to a list or segment in Klaviyo.</p>\n<p>For lists and segments, you can either add tags when creating a list or segment, or you can add tags retroactively when they are already built in your account. This article will cover both methods.</p>\n<h3 id=\"h_01JDX07SS3PW2TSHJE445KGPCQ\">Why use tags?</h3>\n<p>In Klaviyo, tags serve as labels that help you efficiently organize and manage items in Klaviyo (i.e., contact lists and segments). By attaching tags to lists and segments, you can quickly categorize and identify specific groups within your audience. For example, you can tag segments to distinguish between existing customers and prospects, or group lists that'll be used for a specific promotions.</p>\n<p>This streamlined organization makes it easier to filter, manage, and collaborate on different audience segments, enhancing your ability to target communications.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JDWZTJBS5TWCCD4HG3VQHR9A\">Add a tag when creating a list or segment</h2>\n<p>To add a tag when creating a list or a segment: </p>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Audience &gt;</strong> <strong>Lists &amp; Segments</strong> tab.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create List/Segment</strong>.</li>\n<li>Choose to either create a list or a segment.</li>\n<li>In the <em>Tags</em> dropdown, select the tag you want to add, or create a new one by typing it into the textbox.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/31422136339867\" alt=\"The Create list modal where you can name and add tags to a new list when you create it.\" width=\"455\" height=\"429\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JDWZTJBSNE1DCT1M4MR5R3V2\">Add a tag retroactively</h2>\n<p>If you want to add tags to lists and segments that are already in your Klaviyo account:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Audience &gt; </strong><strong>Lists &amp; Segments</strong>.</li>\n<li>Click the checkboxes next to any lists and segments that you want to apply tags to.</li>\n<li>Click the <strong>Add/Remove</strong> <strong>Tags</strong> dropdown at the top of the page.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Add Tags</strong>.<strong><br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28720670350747\" alt=\"Add tags to a list or lists retroactively\"><br></strong>\n</li>\n<li>Click the dropdown under <em>Tags</em> in the modal that appears.</li>\n<li>Select existing tags or input a new tag to create it.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Add Tags</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JDWZTJBT0X679SXVKK0NS7K7\">Additional resources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360025834271\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Understanding tags in Klaviyo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://community.klaviyo.com/lists-segments-and-profiles-35/tags-what-are-they-10143#:~:text=They're%20useful%20for%20managing,use%20tags%20to%20filter%20them.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">What are tags?</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005061447\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Understanding lists and segments</a></li>\n</ul>",
